## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.putMessage(null)` fails when the enhanced-for loop
starts, with `NullPointerException` and no queue or counter changes. Rust now
exposes `put_message_nullable`; `None` returns `ProcessQueueError::NullMessageList`
before mutation, while a present slice delegates to the existing method.

The invoked Java facade fixture records the exception class and unchanged
count, size, and tree. The Rust facade comparison checks those outcomes.
